course: dictionary
lesson: 7895
title: Rapeseed: a word from the fields
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things you may never have seen. Rapeseed is one of them. The context can help: «Rapeseed and sunflowers make seeds that are pressed into cooking oil, and the yellow rapeseed fields are busy with bees in spring.» Rapeseed is grown for its seeds, and it is planted in fields.
explain: The sentence gives you more clues. Sunflowers and rapeseed both make seeds, and both are used for oil. The fields are yellow and full of bees in spring, so rapeseed must be a plant with yellow flowers.
explain: Ask yourself what word would fit. Then test your meaning in the sentence. If you read «the yellow plant fields are busy with bees in spring» and it still makes sense, your meaning is probably right.
fact: Rapeseed is a plant with bright yellow flowers, grown in fields for its seeds.
fact: The oil pressed from rapeseed seeds is rapeseed oil, a common cooking oil.
fact: In Canada, the USA and Australia, rapeseed oil is called canola oil.
fact: Rapeseed is related to turnips and cabbages, and its name comes from Latin «rapum», meaning turnip.
fact: Rapeseed is also used for animal feed and biofuel.
exercise: «Rapeseed and sunflowers make seeds that are pressed into cooking oil.» What is rapeseed? | A kind of cooking pan | A type of sunflower with black petals | *A plant with bright yellow flowers, grown for its seeds | A bee that lives in fields
exercise: «Rapeseed and sunflowers make seeds that are pressed into cooking oil.» Find and copy the word that means squeezed. | sunflowers | seeds | *pressed | cooking
exercise: «Canola» is a type of rapeseed bred in Canada. Which country is canola linked with? | Peru | Egypt | *Canada | Japan
test: The oil pressed from rapeseed seeds is a common cooking oil. What is it called in Canada, the USA and Australia? | Olive oil | *Canola oil | Sunflower oil | Turnip oil
test: The name rapeseed comes from the Latin word «rapum». What does «rapum» mean? | Yellow | Field | *Turnip | Seed
exam: Which is NOT a use of the rapeseed crop named in the lessons? | Animal feed | Cooking oil | Biofuel | *Making bricks
